# Every text file is LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# The repository half was already true: before this file existed, all 225 text
# blobs were LF and not one was CRLF. What was not true was the working tree.
# `core.autocrlf` is true on the machine this is developed on, so checkout wrote
# CRLF to disk and commit converted it back, and the round trip was invisible in
# every diff.
#
# It was not invisible to Prettier, whose `endOfLine` default is `lf`. A local
# `npm run format:check` reported 53 files that CI reads as clean, which is a
# gate that cannot be used: the real failures are in the noise. Two of them
# reached CI on #19 for exactly that reason.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than `text=auto` alone, because `text=auto` normalises the
# blob and leaves the working copy to `core.autocrlf`, which is the half that
# was already fine and the half that was broken respectively.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The four files that are not text. `text=auto` infers this from content and
# would leave them alone anyway; saying it outright means a byte sequence that
# happens to look textual can never corrupt one of them.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
